"Translate returns only gibberish on writing from Earth."
"In the first week, a Disintegrate beam takes Nathan's arm; it is healed later."
"A Questor would not have lost an arm to Disintegrate at all."
"Badud holds Reverse Time; Brox had a counter that kept his memory through it."
"Badud also has a black-hole spell and a radiation spell built in pulses in a concave unit."
"Later, Stella names her spell Hydrabane after killing a hydra eel with it."
"Hydrabane is hungry purple wizardry fire that burns the air and grows as it flies."
"Hydrabane burns stone like sawdust and even burns corrupted death mana."
"Stella's first Hydrabane nearly destroyed the city of Litcliff."
"Later, Stella casts lasers by exciting gas with electricity and sends lightning down the beam."
"Later, Stella's storm spell uses wizardry to move heat and drive a gyre of wind miles wide."
"Later, Stella's wind spell carries a group at a few hundred miles an hour."
"Later, Stella wraps a group in a conductive layer that acts as a Faraday cage."
"Later, Stella holds an incomplete triple crystallized shield ready to cast at once."
"Later, Stella opens gates as a spinning ring of fire; a long gate costs a hill's worth of power."
"Later, Stella can cast a near-fusing plasma beam."
"Later, Mirus casts swarms of force blades, localized time spells and disintegrate at speed."
"Later, Mirus casts a dome of mana threads that counters damaging spells from outside."
"Later, Badud's Reverse Time, trapped in antimagic, resonates and implodes."
"Later, Kamus's hand spell drains Stamina and Focus with each touch and paralyzes."
